# Performance.mark() API Reference

## Overview
The `mark()` method creates a named `PerformanceMark` object representing a high-resolution timestamp marker in the browser's performance timeline. It's widely available across browsers since September 2017.

**Available in:** Web Workers

## Syntax
```javascript
mark(name)
mark(name, markOptions)
```

## Parameters

### `name` (required)
- **Type:** String
- **Description:** Name of the mark. Must not match any property of the deprecated `PerformanceTiming` interface.

### `markOptions` (optional)
An object with the following properties:

| Property | Type | Description |
|----------|------|-------------|
| `detail` | Any (structured-cloneable) | Arbitrary metadata. Defaults to `null`. |
| `startTime` | DOMHighResTimeStamp | Custom timestamp (defaults to `performance.now()`). Must not be negative. |
| `devtools` | Object (Experimental) | Chrome DevTools Extensibility API data |
| `dataType` | String (Experimental) | Must be set to `"marker"` |
| `color` | String (Experimental) | Color designation: `"primary"`, `"secondary"`, `"tertiary"`, `"error"` (with `-light`/`-dark` variants) |
| `properties` | Array (Experimental) | Key-value pairs for metadata |
| `tooltipText` | String (Experimental) | Short description for tooltip |

## Return Value
Returns the `PerformanceMark` entry that was created.

## Exceptions

- **`SyntaxError`:** Thrown if `name` matches a `PerformanceTiming` property
- **`TypeError`:** Thrown if `startTime` is negative

## Usage Examples

### Basic Named Markers
```javascript
performance.mark("login-started");
performance.mark("login-finished");
const videoMarker = performance.mark("video-loaded");
```

### Markers with Details
```javascript
performance.mark("login-started", {
  detail: "Login started using the login button in the top menu."
});

performance.mark("login-started", {
  detail: { htmlElement: myElement.id }
});
```

### Custom Start Time
```javascript
performance.mark("start-checkout", {
  startTime: 20.0
});

performance.mark("login-button-pressed", {
  startTime: myEvent.timeStamp
});
```

### DevTools Extensibility API
```javascript
performance.mark("Image Upload", {
  detail: {
    devtools: {
      dataType: "marker",
      color: "secondary",
      properties: [
        ["Image Size", "2.5MB"],
        ["Upload Destination", "Cloud Storage"]
      ],
      tooltipText: "Processed image uploaded"
    }
  }
});
```

### Reserved Names (Throws Error)
```javascript
performance.mark("navigationStart");
// SyntaxError: "navigationStart" is part of the PerformanceTiming interface
```

## Browser Compatibility
✅ **Baseline: Widely available** - Available across browsers since September 2017

See full compatibility details on [MDN Browser Compatibility Table](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/Performance/mark#browser_compatibility)

## Related Methods
- `performance.clearMarks()` - Remove marks
- `performance.measure()` - Measure between marks
- `performance.getEntriesByType('mark')` - Retrieve mark entries

